+/********* Decoding images no larger than they can be shown *********/
+
+/**
+ * The size an image should be decoded to.
+ *
+ * Nothing can be shown at more detail than the screen holds, so an
+ * image decoded at its full size spends memory that buys nothing. A
+ * page of thumbnails, each a photograph the camera took, is how a
+ * small machine runs out of heap.
+ *
+ * The limit is the max_image_width and max_image_height options, in
+ * pixels; either at zero means no limit in that direction.
+ *
+ * \param width        The image's own width.
+ * \param height       The image's own height.
+ * \param dest_width   Updated with the width to decode to.
+ * \param dest_height  Updated with the height to decode to.
+ * \return true if the image should be decoded smaller than it is.
+ */
+bool image_cache_decode_size(int width, int height,
+			     int *dest_width, int *dest_height);
+
+/**
+ * A smaller copy of a bitmap, or NULL.
+ *
+ * Averages each block of source pixels the destination pixel covers,
+ * which is what keeps a shrunken photograph from coming out speckled.
+ * The source is left alone; the caller owns both bitmaps afterwards.
+ *
+ * \param bitmap       The bitmap to shrink.
+ * \param dest_width   The width to shrink it to.
+ * \param dest_height  The height to shrink it to.
+ * \return the new bitmap, or NULL if it could not be made.
+ */
+void *image_cache_shrink(void *bitmap, int dest_width, int dest_height);
+
 /********* Image content handler generic cache callbacks ************/
 
 /**
